f'(x) =\underset{h \to 0}{\lim}\frac{f(x +h) -f(x)}{h} & Formula\~for\~a\~derivative \\ =\underset{h \to 0}{\lim}\frac{(x +h)^2 -100(x +h) -(x^2 -100x)}{h} & Substitute\~f(x +h)\~and\~f(x) . \\ =\underset{h \to 0}{\lim}\frac{x^2 +2xh +h^2 -100x -100h -x^2 +100x}{h} & Multiply\~polynomials,\~distribute . \\ =\underset{h \to 0}{\lim}\frac{2xh +h^2 -100h}{h} & Collect\~like\~terms . \\ =\underset{h \to 0}{\lim}\frac{\overwrite{h}{\senwline}(2x +h -100)}{\overwrite{h}{\senwline}} & Factor\~and\~cancel\~like\~terms . \\ =\underset{h \to 0}{\lim}2x +h -100 & Simplify . \\ =(2x -100) & Evaluate\~when\~h =0. \\ f'(x) =2x -100 & Formula\~for\~marginal\~cost \\ f'(200) =2(200) -100 =300 & Evaluate\~for\~200\~units .
